 62SC c  2018Ta17: {+62}Sc formed by fragmentation of {+70}Zn{+30+} beam at 345 
 62SC2c  MeV/nucleon from RIKEN-RIBF accelerator complex. Rotating target of    
 62SC3c  {+9}Be of 15 mm thickness were located at the BigRIPS two-stage ion    
 62SC4c  separator. Particle identification (PID) was achieved by measuring     
 62SC5c  time of flight (tof), energy loss (|DE), total kinetic energy (TKE),   
 62SC6c  and magnetic rigidity (B|r) through event by event analysis of         
 62SC7c  reaction products. Particles of interest were stopped in a 76-mm thick 
 62SC8c  CsI crystal after passing through six 1-mm thick silicon p-i-n diodes, 
 62SC9c  while the magnetic rigidity (B|r) of the fragments was reconstructed   
 62SCAc  from position and angle measurements at foci using two sets of         
 62SCBc  position-sensitive parallel plate avalanche counters (PPACs).          
 62SCCc  Optimization was done using LISE{+++} simulation code.                 
 62SC d  No theory references for structure or decay in the NSR database.       
