 62TI c  2009Ta24, 2009Ta05: {+62}Ti identified by fragmentation of {+76}Ge beam
 62TI2c  at 132 MeV/nucleon with Be and W targets at NSCL facility using A1900  
 62TI3c  fragment separator combined with S800 analysis beam line to form a two-
 62TI4c  stage separator system. The transmitted fragments were analyzed        
 62TI5c  event-by-event in terms of momentum and particle identification. The   
 62TI6c  nuclei of interest were stopped in eight Si PIN diodes (50x50 mm{+2})  
 62TI7c  which provided measurement of energy loss, nuclear charge and total    
 62TI8c  kinetic energy. The time-of-flight of each particle that reached the   
 62TI9c  detector stack was measured in four different ways using plastic       
 62TIAc  scintillators, Si detectors, and parallel-plate avalanche counters.    
 62TIBc  The simultaneous measurement of |DE signals, magnetic rigidity, total  
 62TICc  kinetic energy and time-of-flight (ToF) provided unambiguous           
 62TIDc  identification of the atomic number, charge state and mass number.     
 62TI c  2020Mi13: measured mass excess using time-of-flight magnetic-rigidity  
 62TI2c  technique at RIBF-RIKEN facility.                                      
 62TI c                                                                         
 62TI c  Theoretical nuclear structure calculations:                            
 62TI c  2022Ho02: calculated quadrupole deformation parameter |b{-2}, S(2n),   
 62TI2c  rms matter radius, hexadecapole deformation parameter |b{-4},          
 62TI3c  difference of the charge square radii, diffuseness parameters,         
 62TI4c  occupation of highly elongated intruder orbitals and effect on         
 62TI5c  quadrupole and hexadecapole deformations using Skyrme-Hartree-Fock     
 62TI6c  method in three-dimensional coordinate space.                          
 62TI c  2022Ko04: calculated ground state energy, charge rms radius using      
 62TI2c  coupled cluster (|a) and ab-initio density functional theory, extended 
 62TI3c  to open-shell deformed nuclei.                                         
 62TI c  2022Ya23: theory: structure: calculated binding energy, charge radius, 
 62TI2c  quadrupole deformation, and pairing energy using relativistic          
 62TI3c  mean-field (RMF) formalism                                             
 62TI c  2021Co14: calculated S(2n), energy of the first 2+ state, effective    
 62TI2c  single-particle energies (ESPEs), neutron-neutron monopole matrix      
 62TI3c  elements using shell-model with an effective Hamiltonian from          
 62TI4c  many-body perturbation theory using {+40}Ca as a closed core, and      
 62TI5c  three-body contributions through density-dependent two-body matrix     
 62TI6c  elements (TBME) derived within a microscopic approach from             
 62TI7c  chiral forces.                                                         
 62TI c  2018Sa40: calculated potential energy curves, T{-1/2}, Q(|b{+-}),      
 62TI2c  |b{+-}n probability, Gamow-Teller strength distributions using         
 62TI3c  constrained HF+BCS with Skyrme force SLy4.                             
 62TI c  2015Wa11: calculated potential energy surfaces, S(2p), excitation      
 62TI2c  energies and B(E2), J|p, neutron and proton single-particle levels     
 62TI3c  using relativistic mean-field + BCS method with |a(P)-PK1 functional.  
 62TI c  2014Co04: calculated energies and B(E2) values of first 2+ state using 
 62TI2c  realistic shell-model calculations with two different model spaces.    
 62TI c  Theoretical calculations: consult the NSR database at for 16 primary   
 62TI2c  references for nuclear structure, and two for decay modes              
 62TI3c  and half-life.                                                         
 62TI c  2012Ca30: calculated energy levels, J|p, electric quadrupole and dipole
 62TI2c  magnetic moments using shell model with FPD6 and GXPF1 interactions.   
 62TI c  2010Le20: calculated levels, J|p, B(E2), quadrupole moment, occupation 
 62TI2c  of the neutron intruder orbitals and percentage of particle-hole       
 62TI3c  excitations using interacting shell-model framework in full {Ipf}      
 62TI4c  valence space based on {+48}Ca core and effective interaction based    
 62TI5c  on G matrix; discussed shell evolution and island of inversion         
 62TI6c  around N=40.                                                           
 62TI c  2009Ga41: calculated single-particle energies, Nilsson diagrams,       
 62TI2c  potential energy curves, neutron and proton pairing energy curves,     
 62TI3c  excitation energies, spectroscopic quadrupole moments, and B(E2) using 
 62TI4c  Hartree-Fock-Bogoliubov (HFB) approach with Gogny D1S effective        
 62TI5c  interaction                                                            
 62TI c  2008Gu03: calculated potential energy surfaces and ground state        
 62TI2c  deformation using relativistic mean field theory.                      
 62TI c  Other theory references: 12 for structure and two for decay in the     
 62TI2c  NSR database, also listed in this dataset as 'document' records.       
