 62TI c  2020Co01: E({+63}V)|?200 MeV/nucleon, secondary {+63}V beam            
 62TI2c  from {+9}Be({+70}Zn,X),E=345 MeV/nucleon primary reaction followed by  
 62TI3c  separation of fragments of interest event-by-event using BigRIPS       
 62TI4c  spectrometer at RIBF-RIKEN. Measured yields of reaction products with  
 62TI5c  E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, cross sections for population of levels in {+62}Ti
 62TI6c  using MINOS device, SAMURAI dipole magnet, Time Projection Chamber     
 62TI7c  (TPC), and DALI2+ array of 226 NaI(Tl) detectors. A total of 1880      
 62TI8c  events corresponding to the production of {+62}Ti reaction were        
 62TI9c  observed. Deduced first 2+ and 4+ levels. Gamma-ray spectra were       
 62TIAc  Doppler corrected. Comparison with large-scale shell model (LSSM)      
 62TIBc  calculations, using symmetry conserving configuration mixing (SCCM) and
 62TICc  Gogny D1S effective interaction, and valence-space in-medium similarity
 62TIDc  renormalization group (VS-IMSRG).                                      
