 62MN c  All the papers are from the same group at GANIL                        
 62MN c  {+62}Cr produced in fragmentation of {+76}Ge{+30+} beam on a {+58}Ni   
 62MN2c  target. LISE3 doubly achromatic spectrometer used to separate          
 62MN3c  fragments, with magnetic rigidity tuned to optimize transmission of    
 62MN4c  {+62}V and {+64}Cr fragments. Transmitted nuclei were identified by    
 62MN5c  three consecutive Si detectors (300, 300 and 1500 microns); first two  
 62MN6c  served for energy loss and time-of-flight measurements, while the last 
 62MN7c  determined their residual energies.                                    
 62MN c  Measured E|g, I|g, I|b, |g|g, |b|g coin., |g(t), lifetimes with four   
 62MN2c  Ge detectors placed around a thick Si telescope. Half-lives determined 
 62MN3c  by fitting procedure involving five parameters: half-lives of mother,  
 62MN4c  daughter and grand-daughter nuclei, the |b-efficiency and the          
 62MN5c  background rate over the counting time.                                
 62MN c  All data are from 2005Ga01, unless otherwise stated                    
