 62MN    COULOMB EXCITATION            2015GA38                  25NDS    202507
 62MN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62MN2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62MN c  2015Ga38: {+62}Mn beam (mixed with {+62}Fe) produced by bombarding a   
 62MN2c  thick UC{-x} target with a 1.4 GeV proton beam at REX-ISOLDE-CERN      
 62MN3c  facility. A 4.0 mg/cm{+2} thick {+109}Ag target was used for safe      
 62MN4c  Coulomb excitation. The scattered projectiles and the recoiling target 
 62MN5c  nuclei were detected using a DSSSD placed downstream from the          
 62MN6c  target position. The |g rays were detected using HPGe detectors of     
 62MN7c  Miniball array. Measured scattered particles, recoiling target         
 62MN8c  nuclei, E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, (particle)|g-coin, (particle)|g|g-coin,   
 62MN9c  (particle)(particle)-coin. Data analyzed using GOSIA2 which allows a   
 62MNAc  simultaneous least-squares fit of matrix elements in the target and    
 62MNBc  projectile systems                                                     
 62MN c  2015Ga38 stated that the 671-ms, (4+) isomer in the {+62}Mn beam was   
 62MN2c  extracted with a much higher intensity than the 92-ms, (1+) activity,  
 62MN3c  as with a >700 ms trapping plus charge breeding time, only the long    
 62MN4c  lived-state is expected to be present at the target position. Relative 
 62MN5c  position of the two |b-decaying states in {+62}Mn (1(+) and 4(+)) was  
 62MN6c  not known until this experiment.                                       
 62MN c  The 418|g in 2015Ga38 is shown as deexciting a state of this energy,   
 62MN2c  as it is not seen in coincidence with any other |g ray. Nearly         
 62MN3c  independent of spin, such an assumption leads to a B(E2)(W.u.)|?30,    
 62MN4c  more than double that of the 2+ to 0+ transition in {+62}Fe, which is  
 62MN5c  considered unlikely. 2015Ga38 thus propose that while the final state  
 62MN6c  of the decay is the (1+), 92-ms state proceeding via the excitation    
 62MN7c  of an intermediate (2+,3+) level. Through GOSIA analysis, comparison   
 62MN8c  of the observed |g-ray yield of 418|g as a function of level-energy    
 62MN9c  difference between the newly-proposed state and the (4+), 671-ms       
 62MNAc  isomeric state plotted with B(E2)(W.u.) ranging from 1|*10{+-10} W.u.  
 62MNBc  to 5 W.u. suggests that the excitation of the intermediate level at    
 62MNCc  an energy of 72 keV {I+8-3}, above the energy of the 671-ms, (4+)      
 62MNDc  isomer, which fixes the relative ordering of the two |b-decaying       
 62MNDc  states in {+62}Mn.                                                     
 62MN c  Sub-barrier Coulomb excitation using 2.86 MeV/nucleon {+62}Mn beam     
 62MN2c  and {+109}Ag target.                                                   
