 62FE c  2011Ro02: measured lifetime of the first 2+ state using recoil-distance
 62FE2c  Doppler shift method (RDDS) in intermediate Coulomb excitation.        
 62FE3c  Beam={+62}Fe, target={+197}Au. Secondary 97.8 MeV/nucleon {+62}Fe beam 
 62FE4c  was produced in the fragmentation of 130 MeV/nucleon {+76}Ge beam with 
 62FE5c  a {+9}Be target at the NSCL-MSU facility. Measurements                 
 62FE4c  based on A1900 fragment separator and S800 spectrograph.               
 62FE5c  E({+62}Fe)=97.8 MeV/nucleon. Target=300 |mm Au foil, degrader=300 |mm  
 62FE6c  Nb foil. Measured Doppler-shifted |g rays using SeGA array of HPGe     
 62FE7c  detectors, and lifetime of the first 2+ state by recoil-distance       
 62FE8c  Doppler-shift method using Koln-NSCL plunger device. Comparisons made  
 62FE9c  with shell-model calculations and systematics of neighboring nuclides. 
 62FE c  2020Av04: beam={+62}Fe at 400-440 MeV/nucleon, produced in             
 62FE2c  fragmentation reaction: {+9}Be({+86}Kr,X),E({+86}Kr)=700-900           
 62FE3c  MeV/nucleon from the SIS-18 heavy-ion synchrotron at the FAIR-GSI      
 62FE4c  facility, followed by the separation of {+62}Fe fragments using        
 62FE5c  the in-flight Fragment Separator (FRS). Measured |g-ray spectra, and   
 62FE6c  angular distributions up to 8 MeV using the AGATA array of five triple 
 62FE7c  and three double clusters of segmented HPGe detectors placed around the
 62FE8c  {+197}Au target. Deduced B(E1) strengths for different energy regions  
 62FE9c  between E|g=3-8 MeV, and compared to microscopic quasi-particle phonon 
 62FEAc  model calculations. The integrated E1 strength between 6 and 8 MeV     
 62FEBc  was deduced as B(E1)=0.0010 e{+2}b {I3}. 2020Av04 noted that no        
 62FECc  valuable feeding to lower states was found in the |g|g-coin spectra    
 62FEDc  and no isomers were detected in the off prompt or in the beam-like     
 62FEEc  implantation spectra.                                                  
