 62FE2c  {+62}Mn. The {+62}Mn beam was produced by bombarding a thick UC{-x}    
 62FE3c  target with a 1.4 GeV proton beam at REX-ISOLDE-CERN                   
 62FE4c  facility. The trapping and charge breeding times were varied to        
 62FE5c  produce the {+62}Fe beam via in-trap method. The final energy of the   
 62FE6c  beam was 2.86 MeV/nucleon. A 4.0 mg/cm{+2} thick {+109}Ag target was   
 62FE7c  used for safe Coulomb excitation. The scattered projectiles and the    
 62FE8c  recoiling target nuclei were detected using a compact-disc shaped      
 62FE9c  DSSSD placed 32.5 mm downstream from the target position. |g-rays      
 62FEAc  were detected using HPGe detectors of Miniball array. Measured:        
 62FEBc  scattered particles, recoiling target nuclei, E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,     
 62FECc  (particle)|g-coin, (particle)(particle)-coin, (particle)|g|g-coin,     
