 62CO cG M$From |g(|q) and |g|g(|q) data in {+26}Mg({+48}Ca,3np2|a|g)           
 62CO2cG (2022Se03), and from |g(|q) for four transitions in                    
 62CO3cG {+48}Ca({+18}O,p3n|g) (1978Wa09). Evaluators assign Q for |DJ=2,       
 62CO4cG quadrupole, and D or D+Q for |DJ=1,0 dipole or dipole+quadrupole.      
 62CO5cG As no long-lived levels have been found, |DJ=2, quadrupole (Q) are     
 62CO6cG likely |DJ=2, E2 and |DJ=1,0 dipole+quadrupole, likely M1+E2.          
 62CO cL E$From |g-ray studies when possible. Energies of levels populated      
 62CO2cL only in particle-transfer reactions taken from {+62}Ni(t,{+3}He) and   
 62CO3cL {+64}Ni(d,|a) for levels below 2.8 MeV, and from {+64}Ni(pol d,|a)     
 62CO4cL for higher energies. Level energies from |g-ray studies are based      
 62CO5cL on fixed energy of 22 keV for the first excited state, without its     
 62CO6cL stated uncertainty of 5 keV.                                           
