 62NI c  {+62}Ni isotope identified in mass spectroscopic data by 1934As04.     
 62NI c  Other Reactions:                                                       
 62NI c  2016Mo15: {+116}Sn({+60}Ni,{+62}Ni),E=245 MeV. Measured Ni-like        
 62NI2c  fragments using PRISMA spectrometer, and |g rays using AGATA           
 62NI3c  demonstrator array of highly segmented Ge detectors at Legnaro         
 62NI4c  accelerator facility. A weak peak at 1173 keV seen, corresponding to   
 62NI5c  transition from the first 2+ state, with deduced yield of <0.00145.    
 62NI6c  No evidence was found for the population of the 2340, 4+ level.        
 62NI c  {+63}Cu(|g,p): 1975We11, 1971We06, 1968Ab10; g.s. and first 2+ levels  
 62NI c  {+65}Zn(n,|a): 1984Em01: E=thermal, FWHM=50-60 keV, measured |s(|q)    
 62NI2c  for g.s. and first 2+ level                                            
 62NI c  {+66}Zn(d,{+6}Li): 1973Ce02: E=27.25 MeV, Si telescopes, FWHM=400 keV, 
 62NI2c  |s(|q) for g.s. and first 2+ state                                     
 62NI c                                                                         
 62NI c  Theoretical structure calculations:                                    
 62NI c  2022Ba29: calculated rms charge radii, isotope shifts using            
 62NI2c  Skyrme and D1MTd Gogny effective interactions.                         
 62NI c  2022Ga13: analyzed experimental investigations of multiple nuclear     
 62NI2c  shape coexistence.                                                     
 62NI c  2022Ko04: calculated ground state energy, charge rms radius using      
 62NI2c  coupled cluster (|a) and ab-initio density functional theory.          
 62NI c  2022Ku16: calculated potential energy surface, binding energy, S(2n),  
 62NI2c  charge, neutron and proton rms radii, neutron skin thickness using     
 62NI3c  Skyrme parameterizations.                                              
 62NI c  2021Hu26: calculated energies of the lowest bands based on the         
 62NI2c  |ng{-9/2}{+2} configuration, root mean square angular momentum         
 62NI3c  components along the medium, short, and long axes of the rotor,        
 62NI4c  valence neutrons, and total angular momentum, probability density      
 62NI5c  profiles for the orientation of the angular momentum on the plane      
 62NI6c  for the doublet bands using covariant density functional theory and    
 62NI7c  quantum particle rotor model; suggested transverse wobbling in {+62}Ni.
 62NI c  2020So01: calculated total binding energy, S(2n), rms charge radius    
 62NI2c  using state-of-the-art no-core shell model and self-consistent         
 62NI3c  Green's function approaches with NN+3N interaction                     
 62NI c  2015Co17: calculated energies of three-phonon levels, B(E2),           
 62NI2c  anharmonic vibrators using leading order (LO) and next-to-leading-order
 62NI3c  (NLO) effective field theory (EFT) for nuclear vibrations, with        
 62NI4c  Bayesian statistics for quantification of theoretical uncertainties.   
 62NI c  2015Fr06: calculated energy levels, J|p, B(E2), signatures for         
 62NI2c  triaxiality using triaxial projected shell Model.                      
 62NI c  Other 33 theoretical structure references from 2018-2022 are listed    
 62NI2c  'document' records in this dataset. Retrieval of the NSR database      
 62NI3c  shows other 230 primary theory references from 1970-2017 related to    
 62NI4c  structure of {+62}Ni.                                                  
