 62NI cL E$From a least-squares fit for levels connected by |g rays; and from   
 62NI2cL {+64}Ni(p,t), {+62}Ni(p,p'), and {+61}Ni(d,p)                          
 62NI3cL for levels not populated in |g-ray studies. Exceptions are noted       
 62NI cL J$For high-spin levels (J>6 or so), assignments are generally based on 
 62NI2cL |DJ and multipolarities for |g transitions deduced from |g(|q) data in 
 62NI3cL {+26}Mg({+48}Ca,2|a4n|g) (2016Al18), combined with band associations.  
 62NI4cL Further, ascending spins with increasing excitation energy are assumed 
 62NI5cL due to the yrast nature of population of levels in heavy-ion in-beam   
 62NI6cL |g-ray spectroscopy. Exceptions are noted.                             
