 62NI    61NI(D,P),(POL D,P)           2023Sp03,1981KA24,1963FU0425NDS    202507
 62NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62NI2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62NI c  J|p({+61}Ni g.s.)=3/2-                                                 
 62NI c  2023Sp03: (d,p),E(d)=16 MeV. Measured proton spectra, |s(|q) using the 
 62NI2c  light-ion focal plane detection system of the FSU Super-Enge Split-Pole
 62NI3c  Spectrograph (Se-SPS) at the 9-MV Tandem van-de-Graaff accelerator at  
 62NI4c  the Florida State University. Target was 427 |mg/cm{+2} thick,         
 62NI5c  self-supporting {+61}Ni metal foil. FWHM=59 keV. Adiabatic Distorted   
 62NI6c  Wave Approximation (ADWA) calculations used for the analysis of spins, 
 62NI7c  parities, and spectroscopic factors using the coupled-channels         
 62NI8c  code CHUCK3. 2023Sp03, in Fig. 8, also present results of angular      
 62NI9c  distribution data from {+62}Ni(|g,|g'), details of which are to appear 
 62NIAc  in a separate publication (ref. 53 in 2023Sp03).                       
 62NI c  2023Sp03: Phys. Rev. C (accepted, June 26, 2023)                       
 62NI c  1981Ka24: (pol d,p),E(d)=12.3 MeV vector- and tensor-polarized beams   
 62NI2c  from Birmingham University Radial Ridge Cyclotron. Measured deuteron   
 62NI3c  spectra, |s(|q), and tensor analyzing powers iT{-11}(|q), T{-20}(|q),  
 62NI4c  T{-22}(|q) using six |DE-E telescopes. Target was 96.6% enriched       
 62NI5c  {+61}Ni with thickness of 1 mg/cm{+2}. FWHM=75 keV. DWBA analysis of   
 62NI6c  |s(|q) and analyzing powers.                                           
 62NI c  1963Fu04: (d,p),E(d)=15 MeV. Measured proton spectra, |s(|q) using a   
 62NI2c  wedge magnetic spectrograph, and photographic emulsion plates. Target  
 62NI3c  was enriched {+61}Ni with a thickness of 2 mg/cm{+2} at the University 
 62NI4c  of Pittsburgh cyclotron. FWHM=45 keV. DWBA analysis of |s(|q) data.    
 62NI5c  This work reported 26 levels up to 6740 keV, with differential cross   
 62NI6c  sections for all the levels, and L-transfers and spectroscopic factors 
 62NI7c  for 16 levels.                                                         
 62NI c  1975ShYO: (d,p),E(d)=13.6 MeV. Measured proton spectra, |s(|q) using   
 62NI2c  Si(Li) detector telescope. Data for g.s. and 1170 level.               
 62NI c  1967Te02: (d,p),E(d)=7-7.5 MeV. Measured deuteron spectra using        
 62NI2c  Harwell single-channel spectrograph. Target was 92.4% enriched {+61}Ni 
 62NI3c  with thickness of 100 |mg/cm{+2}. FWHM=15 keV. No |s(|q) data were     
 62NI4c  reported. In Table 6, authors report 97 levels populated in (d,p) and  
 62NI5c  in {+62}Ni(p,p') reaction. However, authors reported level energies    
 62NI6c  only from (p,p') data, with the statement that all fully-resolved      
 62NI7c  levels were observed in (d,p) as well. Differences between the two     
 62NI8c  sets of data were due to resolution differences in the two reactions,  
 62NI9c  with somewhat better resolution in (p,p'). See also {+62}Ni(p,p')      
 62NIAc  dataset.                                                               
 62NI c  1967Al04: (d,p),E(d)=7.0 MeV. Measured deuteron spectra using a        
 62NI2c  magnetic spectrograph. The results of this unpublished work are        
 62NI3c  tabulated in 1967Ve10 and 1974Ve13 evaluations of A=62 nuclei.         
 62NI c  1966So01: (d,p),E(d)=15 MeV. Measured deuteron spectra, |s(|q) using   
 62NI2c  a magnetic spectrometer and a triple scintillator at the University of 
 62NI3c  Pittsburgh cyclotron facility. Data for the g.s. and 1180, 2+ state.   
 62NI4c  DWBA analysis of |s(|q) data.                                          
 62NI c  1965Bo36: (d,p),E(d)=6 MeV. Measured proton spectra using a magnetic   
 62NI2c  spectrograph. The results of this work are tabulated in                
 62NI3c  1967Ve10 evaluation of A=62 nuclei.                                    
 62NI c  1975Ch03: (d,p),E(d)=27.5 MeV. Measured continuous proton spectrum from
 62NI2c  5 MeV to 22 MeV at the IPN, Lyon synchrocyclotron. Deuteron break-up   
 62NI3c  mechanism and phase space calculations.                                
 62NI cL E$From 2023Sp03, unless otherwise stated. Values from other studies    
 62NI2cL are listed under comments. Note that many levels in this dataset, and  
 62NI3cL probably more, were observed by 1967Te02, but the authors neither      
 62NI4cL listed level energies from (d,p), nor displayed a proton spectrum.     
 62NI5cL Level energies (with an uncertainty of 10 keV) were given by 1967Te02  
 62NI6cL only for {+62}Ni(p,p'), which can be consulted for details.            
 62NI cL E(X)$Level is not reported by 2023Sp03                                 
 62NI cL J$As listed by 2023Sp03. For L=1, 2p{-3/2} neutron transfer,           
 62NI2cL J|p=0+,1+,2+ from p{-3/2} orbital for {+61}Ni g.s. and                 
 62NI3cL Pauli exclusion principle. Several assignments are from                
 62NI4cL 2012Ni08 evaluation of A=62 nuclei.                                    
 62NI cL J(g)$From intensity ratio, J=1 or (1) assigned by 2023Sp03 from        
 62NI2cL {+62}Ni(|g,|g') in a paper to be published (ref. 53 in this work);     
 62NI3cL partial data from (|g,|g') are presented in Fig. 8d of 2023Sp03.       
 62NI cL L$From 2023Sp03, based on ADWA analysis, except as noted. Values from  
 62NI4cL other studies are listed in comments.                                  
 62NI CL S$LABEL=(2J+1)S                                                        
 62NI cL S$From 2023Sp03, except as noted. 2023Sp03 give (2J+1)S values when    
 62NI2cL a level could not be assigned a single value, and S value when a       
 62NI3cL single J|p is assigned. Evaluators have multiplied the latter values   
 62NI4cL by (2J+1), so that all the values are listed as (2J+1)S. The S values  
 62NI5cL from 2023Sp03 are listed under comments. Authors consider transfer     
 62NI6cL configuration for the neutron as 2p{-3/2} for L=1, 2d{-5/2} for        
 62NI7cL L=2, 1f{-5/2} for L=3, and 1g{-9/2} for L=4. The (2J+1)S values from   
 62NI8cL other studies are listed under comments. Note that large differences   
 62NI9cL exist between different studies. Perhaps different formulations or     
 62NIAcL normalization (scaling) factors for the (2J+1)S values have been used. 
