 62NI c  1969Be20: (p,p'),E=12 MeV from ce(N) Saclay-SPNBE tandem Van de Graaff 
 62NI2c  accelerator. Measured E(p), I(p), E|g, I|g, p|g-coin using a cooled    
 62NI3c  surface barrier silicon detector for protons, and NaI(Tl) detector for 
 62NI4c  |g rays. Target was |?99% enriched {+62}Ni with a thickness of 250     
 62NI5c  |mg/cm{+2} and backing of 30 |mg carbon. FWHM|?20 keV for protons.     
 62NI c  2019Ev01 (also 2018Ev01): E(p)=9.2 MeV from the 14UD pelletron         
 62NI2c  accelerator at the Australian National University. Target=1.3 mg/cm{+2}
 62NI3c  enriched {+62}Ni. Measured E|g, |g(|q) using the CEASAR array of nine  
 62NI4c  Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors. The conversion electrons were       
 62NI5c  measured using superconducting electron spectrometer Super-e with      
 62NI6c  a set of six 9-mm thick Si(Li) detectors for electrons, and a single   
 62NI7c  Compton-suppressed HPGe detector to enable simultaneous measurement    
 62NI8c  of electrons and |g rays. Data for E0 admixed transition from the      
 62NI9c  second 2+ state, and the first excited state. Comparison with          
 62NIAc  configuration-interaction (CI) shell-model calculations                
 62NI c  1981Pa10: E(p)=6.9 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, Ice, p|g-coin using Ge(Li)  
 62NI2c  detectors for |g rays, magnetic spectrometer and Si(Li) detector       
 62NI3c  for conversion electrons at the University of Jyvaskyla cyclotron.     
