 62NI    62NI(A,A')                    1982KU18                  25NDS    202507
 62NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62NI2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62NI c  1982Ku18: E(|a)=28.5 MeV. Measured E|a, |s(|q) using two thick         
 62NI2c  silicon surface barrier detectors with FWHM=70 keV at Kyoto University 
 62NI3c  cyclotron facility. DWBA analysis of |s(|q) distributions.             
 62NI c  1970Br07 (also 1966Br19, 1963Br29, 1963Ba45): E(|a)=44 MeV. Measured   
 62NI2c  E|a, |s(|q) using a magnetic spectrometer, as well as lithium-drifted  
 62NI3c  solid-state detectors with or without surface barrier with FWHM=180 keV
 62NI4c  at the Saclay fixed energy cyclotron. Data for g.s., 1170, 2+; 2300    
 62NI5c  (4+ and 2+); 3200, 2+ and 3690, 3- states. Deduced deformation         
 62NI6c  parameters and transition probabilities using Austern-Blair model      
 62NI7c  analysis.                                                              
 62NI c  1965Ho08, 1965Ha27: E(|a)=25,33,50,85,100 MeV; measured E|a, |s(|q);   
 62NI2c  deduced transition probabilities and matrix elements. Data for 1172,   
 62NI3c  2340, 3777 and 5650 levels.                                            
 62NI c  1964Ha24: E|a=50, 85 MeV. Measured E|a for 12 levels up to 4670 keV    
 62NI c  1963Br13: E(|a)=43 MeV. Measured E|a using a lithium-drifted           
 62NI2c  solid-state detector at the Argonne 60-in. cyclotron facility. Data    
 62NI3c  for nine levels up to 6480 keV                                         
 62NI c  Others:                                                                
 62NI c  1979PaZO (abstract): E(|a)=29, 40, 45, 50 MeV. Measured |s(|q);        
 62NI2c  deduced |b{-2} for the first 2+ state.                                 
 62NI c  1975Al34, 1975Al12: E(|a)=27.2 MeV. Measured E|a, |s(|q). Deduced      
 62NI2c  |b{-2} for the first 2+ and |b{-3} for the first 3- state.             
 62NI c  1975Al06: E(|a)=18 MeV. The emitted |a particles were detected using   
 62NI2c  two telescopes of surface-barrier charged particle detectors at the    
 62NI3c  University of Pittsburgh Van de Graaff accelerator. Measured continuous
 62NI4c  spectrum, deduced double-differential cross section,                   
 62NI5c  compound-nucleus contribution to cross section, and level density.     
 62NI c  1974Tr04: E(|a)=18-27 MeV. Measured E|a, |s(|q) using multidetector    
 62NI2c  array of eight Si surface-barrier detectors with FWHM=200 keV at       
 62NI3c  the Munich MP tandem accelerator facility. Data for g.s. and first 2+. 
 62NI4c  Coupled-channel analysis with optical-model parameters.                
 62NI5c  Deduced deformation parameter for the first 2+ state.                  
 62NI c  1974Co28: E(|a)=24.3-32.3 MeV. Measured E|a, |s(|q) using a Si         
 62NI2c  surface-barrier detector with FWHM=100 keV at the CSIR, Pretoria       
 62NI3c  variable energy cyclotron. DWBA analysis. Data for the g.s., first 2+  
 62NI4c  and first 3- states.                                                   
 62NI c  1973Bi12: E(|a)=166 MeV. Measured E|a, |s(|q) using a magnetic         
 62NI2c  spectrometer and a plastic-scintillator hodoscope with FWHM=900 keV    
 62NI3c  at the Orsay IPN synchrocyclotron. Data for the first 2+ and           
 62NI4c  first 3- states. DWBA analysis. Deduced B(E2) and B(E3)                
 62NI c  1972Re15: E(|a)=104 MeV. Measured E|a, |s(|q) using Si(Li) detector    
 62NI2c  with FWHM=250-300 keV at the Karlsruhe synchrocyclotron facility.      
 62NI3c  Data for g.s. and the first 2+ state.                                  
 62NI c  1972Lu03, 1972Lu09: E(|a)=16.2, 17 MeV. The emitted |a particles were  
 62NI2c  detected by thin surface-barrier detectors at the University of        
 62NI3c  Rochester tandem Van de Graaff generator. Measured continuous |a       
 62NI4c  spectrum, deduced differential cross sections, and level density.      
 62NI c  1966Fu12: E(|a)=21 MeV. Measured E|a; deduced deformation parameter    
 62NI2c  for the first 2+ state                                                 
 62NI c  Most prominent peaks in spectral Fig. 2 of 1982Ku18 are the g.s.,      
 62NI2c  1170 keV, 2+ and 3750 keV, 3-.                                         
