 62CU c  Theoretical nuclear structure calculations:                            
 62CU c  2022An16: calculated rms charge radii using the relativistic mean field
 62CU2c  (RMF) model.                                                           
 62CU c  2020Am03: calculated levels, J|p, S(n), Q(|b{+-})values using          
 62CU2c  neutron-proton interacting boson-fermion-fermion model.                
 62CU c  2020Bo22: calculated charge radii using the self-consistent theory of  
 62CU2c  finite Fermi systems and energy density functionals (EDFs).            
 62CU c  2011Vi03, 2010Vi07: calculated levels, J|p, g factors, quadrupole      
 62CU2c  moments using shell model with GXPF1A effective interaction.           
 62CU c  2004Ho08: calculated magnetic dipole and electric quadrupole moments   
 62CU2c  using shell model.                                                     
 62CU c  2003Ji09: calculated deformation, superdeformed configurations using   
 62CU2c  relativistic mean-field theory.                                        
 62CU c  1999Ca29: calculated levels, J|p using shell model.                    
 62CU c  1997Si01: calculated levels, one-nucleon transfer spectroscopic        
 62CU2c  factors using interacting Boson-Fermion-Fermion Model.                 
 62CU c  1987Hu07: calculated levels, J|p, supersymmetry quantum numbers        
 62CU2c  using Boson-fermion dynamical symmetry and supersymmetry for odd-odd   
 62CU3c  nuclei with U(|b)(5) Boson Limit.                                      
 62CU c  1979Ch01: calculated energies of two-nucleon high spin states, coupling
 62CU2c  to maximum spin of two nucleons using shell model.                     
 62CU c  1977Ko02: calculated levels, binding energies using shell model.       
 62CU c  1975Wa29: calculated levels, J|p using shell model.                    
 62CU c  1968Ph04: calculated levels, magnetic dipole moment using              
 62CU2c  configuration-mixing calculation                                       
 62CU d  Other theoretical nuclear structure calculations:                      
