 62CU  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62CU2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62CU c  2022Lu01: E({+54}Cr)=67 MeV beam from the Separated Sector Cyclotron of
 62CU2c  iThemba LABS. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin and |g|g(|q)(ADO ratios) at 
 62CU3c  90|' and 135|', |g|g(linear polarization) using AFRODITE array         
 62CU4c  consisting of eleven Compton-suppressed clover detectors and three     
 62CU5c  low-energy photon spectrometers (LEPS) for |g detection. Comparison    
 62CU6c  with theoretical predictions from tilted axis cranking (TAC) covariant 
 62CU7c  density functional theory (CDFT).                                      
 62CU cG $Typical ADO ratios: |?1.2 for stretched quadrupole and |?0.8 for      
 62CU2cG |DJ=1, pure dipole transitions.                                        
 62CU cG E(x)$Probably belongs to {+62}Cu, as observed in coincident spectrum   
 62CU2cG with gate on 243.5|g+349.7|g+386.0|g, but not placed by 2022Lu01       
 62CU cG M$Assigned by evaluators based on angular anisotropy (ADO ratios), and 
 62CU2cG linear polarizations data in 2022Lu01                                  
 62CU cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data. The dataset is poorly fitted     
 62CU2cL with reduced |h{+2}=9.1 as compared to critical |h{+2}=1.5, with 12    
 62CU3cL |g-ray energies with deviations of more than 3|s from the fitted       
 62CU4cL values or level-energy differences, as indicated in comments.          
 62CU cL J$As given in 2022Lu01, based on angular anisotropy (ADO ratios), and  
 62CU2cL linear polarizations for selected transitions. Most assignments are the
 62CU3cL same as in earlier literature, except that some are given as firm      
 62CU4cL values                                                                 
