 62CU4c  two NaI(T1) detectors at HMI, Berlin. No |g-ray intensities or         
 62CU5c  branching ratios were given. Levels given up to 1142 keV.              
 62CU c  1984Ch25 (also 1977Ch04): (p,n|g),E(p)=5.5-7.3 MeV. Measured E|g,      
 62CU2c  |g(|q), |g|g-coin using Ge(Li) detectors at the 7 MV Van de Graaff     
 62CU3c  accelerator of Centre de Recherches Nucleaires, Strasbourg. Results of 
 62CU4c  |g(|q) are given only in terms of deduced mixing ratios |d. No |g-ray  
 62CU5c  intensities or branching ratios were given. Levels given up to         
 62CU6c  1843 keV. 1977Ch04 work was mainly for {+59}Co(|a,n|g){+62}Cu reaction 
 62CU c  1970Da15: (p,n|g),E(p)=4.7-5.9 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,      
 62CU2c  |g(|q) using Ge(Li) detectors at the ANU tandem Van de Graaff          
 62CU3c  accelerator. Comparison with predictions of the compound-nucleus       
 62CU4c  statistical model. Authors give |g-branching ratios for                
 62CU5c  levels up to 916 keV.                                                  
 62CU c  1975SeZF: (p,n|g),E(p)=6.0 MeV, measured E|g, I|g using Ge(Li) detector
 62CU c  1972BaUS: (p,n|g),E(p)=6.0 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g using Ge(Li)         
 62CU2c  detector. Levels given up to 1354 keV.                                 
 62CU c  1974Ca14: (p,n|g),E(p)=5.32-5.51 MeV. Measured level T{-1/2} by DSAM   
 62CU2c  using Ge(Li) detector at the ANU Tandem accelerator facility.          
