 62ZN c  {+62}Zn produced and identified in deuteron and {+3}He bombardment     
 62ZN2c  of Cu (1948Mi12), who also measured half-life                          
 62ZN c  Other reactions:                                                       
 62ZN c  1997Fo03: {+62}Ni(|p{++},|p{+-}),E=140-230 MeV, measured |s(|q)        
 62ZN c  1993Be02: {+62}Ni(|p{++},|p{+-}),E=293.4 MeV, measured |s(|q)          
 62ZN c  1979ShZN: {+58}Ni({+14}N,{+10}B),E=155 MeV, measured |s(|q), DWBA      
 62ZN c  1977Gr03: {+58}Ni(|a,p),E=6.26-9.12 MeV in steps of 20 keV, excitation 
 62ZN2c  functions measured to find resonances of large |a width. The           
 62ZN3c  spectra show a large number of alpha-particle resonances, but their    
 62ZN4c  energies are not listed. Differential cross sections were measured     
 62ZN5c  at three angles. No evidence was found for levels with very large      
 62ZN6c  |a widths; observed |a width was concentrated in a small number        
 62ZN7c  of states, in qualitative agreement with the predictions of a weak     
 62ZN8c  coupling shell model                                                   
 62ZN c  1976Ca06: {+64}Zn(|g,2n),E=8-30 MeV; measured |s, GDR width            
 62ZN c  1970Co25: {+64}Zn(|g,2n),E=12-40 MeV; measured |s, GDR                 
 62ZN c  Mass measurement: 2006Er03 (Penning trap method)                       
 62ZN c  2013Zu01: measured quadrupole interaction frequencies for a {+62}Zn    
 62ZN2c  probe using on-line perturbed angular correlation (PAC) and positron   
 62ZN3c  annihilation spectroscopy (PAS), with 30-keV radioactive {+62}Zn beam  
 62ZN4c  produced at the HI-13 tandem accelerator of the China Institute of     
 62ZN5c  Atomic Energy (CIAE).                                                  
 62ZN c  2019Go35: {+30}Si({+32}Si,X){+62}Zn{+*},E=75,86,98,110 MeV; measured   
 62ZN2c  E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, n|g-coin for analysis of decay of compound nucleus
 62ZN c  Theoretical nuclear structure calculations:                            
 62ZN c  2022Mi15: calculated energies of low-lying 0+, 2+, 4+ states, and B(E2)
 62ZN c  2022Ko04: calculated ground state energy, charge rms radius using      
 62ZN2c  coupled cluster (|a) and ab-initio density functional theory.          
 62ZN c  2022Yo05: calculated excitation energies of the high-spin rotational   
 62ZN2c  bands, moments of inertia of superdeformed bands, quadrupole           
 62ZN3c  deformation, and possible occurrence of hyperdeformed states using     
 62ZN4c  cranked Skyrme-Khon-Sham calculations.                                 
 62ZN c  2018Ja02: calculated levels, J|p, and B(E2) using IBM-3.               
 62ZN c  2016Ra37: calculated levels, occupation numbers, B(E2) using           
 62ZN2c  shell model with NuShellX code.                                        
 62ZN c  2016Sa34: calculated levels, J|p, HF energies, quadrupole deformation, 
 62ZN2c  triaxiality parameter, neutron and proton s.p. alignments using        
 62ZN3c  no-core-configuration-interaction (NCCI) model                         
 62ZN c  2005Ji06: calculated binding energy, radius, deformation using         
 62ZN2c  relativistic mean-field approach                                       
