 62ZN6cL The (|+) notation refers to |a=+1/2 and |a=-1/2 signature.             
 62ZN cL $Note that: configurations for bands are from Fig. 21 in 2012Ge04 in   
 62ZN2cL {+28}Si({+36}Ar,2p|g),{+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g) data with the following  
 62ZN3cL nomenclature based on cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky formalism,            
 62ZN4cL and relative to {+56}Ni (N=Z=28) core:                                 
 62ZN cL $|p[(1f{-7/2}){+-p1}(fp){+p3}(1g{-9/2}){+p2}] abbreviated as           
 62ZN2cL |p[p1,p2(|+)], where p3=2+p1-p2, + for |a=+1/2, - for |a=-1/2          
 62ZN3cL for odd number of {Ifp} protons p3.                                    
 62ZN cL $|n[(1f{-7/2}){+-n1}(fp){+n3}(1g{-9/2}){+n2}] abbreviated as           
 62ZN2cL |n[n1,n2(|+)], where n3=4+n1+n2, + for |a=+1/2, - for |a=-1/2          
 62ZN3cL for odd number of {Ifp} neutrons n3.                                   
 62ZN cL E$From least-squares fit to the E|g data from |g-ray studies.          
 62ZN2cL Reduced |h{+2}=0.61, with only two E|g values poorly fitted:           
 62ZN3cL 3425.0|g from 3424 level to the g.s., and 2870.5|g from 5210 level.    
 62ZN4cL Energies of levels populated only in particle-transfer data, are from  
 62ZN5cL averages of available values of comparable precision.                  
 62ZN cL E(Z)$No deexciting |g ray(s) from this level                           
 62ZN cL J$Unless otherwise specified, J|p assignments are from |g|g(|q)(DCO)   
 62ZN2cL data, deexcitation pattern, band assignments, and comparison with      
 62ZN3cL cranked-shell model calculations in 2012Ge04 from the reaction:        
 62ZN4cL {+28}Si({+36}Ar,2p|g),{+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g). Above 6.1 MeV           
 62ZN5cL excitation, except for three levels populated in ({+12}C,{+10}Be), all 
 62ZN6cL the assignments are from {+28}Si({+36}Ar,2p|g),{+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g).
 62ZN7cL Most of these are placed in parentheses, as in evaluators' opinion,    
 62ZN8cL strong arguments for definite assignments seem lacking in the absence  
 62ZN9cL of definite electric or magnetic nature of multipolarity assignments   
 62ZNAcL from |g-ray polarization data, or level lifetime measurements. Further,
 62ZNBcL ascending spins with increasing excitation energy are assumed due to   
 62ZNCcL the yrast nature of population of levels in heavy-ion in-beam          
 62ZNDcL |g-ray spectroscopy. Values of L-transfers are from 0+ targets in all  
 62ZNEcL the particle-transfer reactions given here.                            
