 62ZN    64ZN(P,T)                     2019LE11,1974HI05,1973KU0525NDS    202507
 62ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62ZN2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62ZN c  2019Le11 (also 2013Le25, 2018Ga22): E(p)=24 MeV from MP tandem Van de  
 62ZN2c  Graaff accelerator at the Maier-Leibnitz-Laboratory (MLL) of           
 62ZN3c  Ludwig-Maximilians-University (LMU) and Technical University of Munich 
 62ZN4c  (TUM) in Garching. Target was |?100 |mg/cm{+2} thick, and >99% enriched
 62ZN5c  in {+64}Zn, with a 10 |mg/cm{+2} carbon backing. Tritons were momentum 
 62ZN6c  analyzed using Q3D magnetic spectrograph, and were detected using a    
 62ZN7c  cathode-strip detector, with FWHM of 10 keV. Measured energies and     
 62ZN8c  intensities of the triton peaks, and differential |s(|q) at eight      
 62ZN9c  angles from 10|' to 50|'. Deduced levels, J, and |p. Comparison with   
 62ZNAc  finite-range, coupled-channel DWBA calculations of |s(|q) using FRESCO 
 62ZNBc  code for calculations of |s(|q), and with ab-initio shell-model        
 62ZNCc  calculations using chiral effective field theory (|hEFT). The          
 62ZNDc  optical-model parameters for proton and triton were chosen to reproduce
 62ZNEc  observed elastic scattering |s(|q) data. Relevance to nuclear structure
 62ZNFc  data for 0+ |) 0+ superallowed Fermi |b decays.                        
 62ZN c  1974Hi05: E=35 MeV, Enge split-pole magnetic spectrograph, measured    
 62ZN2c  |s(|q) from 3 to 90|' (lab), photographic emulsions, FWHM=20 keV. DWBA 
 62ZN3c  analysis of |s(|q) distributions. Uncertainty in excitation energy is  
 62ZN4c  given as 10 keV up to about 4.2 MeV, and 20-30 keV for higher levels   
 62ZN c  1973Ku05: E=51.9 MeV, 98.3% enriched target, broad range magnetic      
 62ZN2c  spectrometer, measured |s(|q) from 4.8 to 44.8|' (lab) in 4|' steps,   
 62ZN3c  FWHM=80 keV. Uncertainties in cross sections=20%. DWBA analysis of     
 62ZN4c  |s(|q) distributions. Uncertainty in excitation energy is given as     
 62ZN5c  20 keV. Differential cross sections listed in Table I of 1973Ku05      
 62ZN6c  are not specified as to the angle. From |s(|q) figures, these          
 62ZN7c  appear to be at 20.8|' for which triton spectrum is shown in Fig. 1.   
 62ZN c  1972Fa08: E=27.5 MeV, 99% enriched target, measured |s(|q) from 8      
 62ZN2c  to 110|' (lab), |DE-E Si telescope, FWHM=80-100 keV, DWBA analysis     
 62ZN3c  of |s(|q) distributions. Deduced transition strengths and enhancement  
 62ZN4c  factors from experimental and calculated (DWBA) cross sections,        
 62ZN5c  assuming 1f{-5/2}{+2} configuration of two neutrons in most cases      
 62ZN c  Others:                                                                
 62ZN c  1988Ca04: analyzed cross-section data for first excited 0+             
 62ZN2c  and g.s.                                                               
 62ZN c  1985Mi06, 1980Or04: E=51.9 MeV. Measured ground state                  
 62ZN2c  transition strength                                                    
 62ZN c  1976Gu08: E=23.3-42.4 MeV, 98.9% enriched target, measured |s(|q) from 
 62ZN2c  12 to 90|'(lab), |DE-E Si detector telescope, FWHM=120 keV. DWBA       
