 62ZN    62GA EC DECAY (116.123 MS)    2020MA59,2008FI07,2008BE2125NDS    202507
 62ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62ZN2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62ZN c  2020Ma59: {+62}Ga produced in the ZrC(p,X),E(p)=479 MeV at the ISAC    
 62ZN2c  facility at TRIUMF. Detected |b{++} particles                          
 62ZN3c  with SCEPTAR array of 20 plastic scintillators. Measured E|g, I|g,     
 62ZN4c  |b|g-, |g|g- and |b|g|g-coin, |g|g(|q) using GRIFFIN array of 16 HPGe  
 62ZN5c  clover detectors, each Compton-suppressed by 20-element BGO detectors, 
 62ZN6c  and SCEPTAR array of plastic scintillators for |b particles. Deduced   
 62ZN7c  precise |b{++}+|e branch to the g.s. of {+62}Zn. Deduced               
 62ZN8c  isospin-symmetry breaking in superallowed Fermi |b decay from          
 62ZN9c  0+ to 0+ state. Deduced isospin-mixing correction |d{-C1}=0.110% {I9}  
 62ZN2c  in {+62}Ga superallowed decay to the excited 0+ states in {+62}Zn, as  
 62ZN3c  compared to evaluated |d{-C1}=0.275% {I55} in 2015Ha07                 
 62ZN c  2008Fi07: {+62}Ga produced in the Zr(p,X) reaction using 500 MeV       
 62ZN2c  protons produced at the ISAC facility at TRIUMF. Detected |b{++}       
 62ZN3c  particles with SCEPTAR array of 20 plastic scintillators. Measured E|g,
 62ZN4c  I|g, |g|g, |b|g coin using 8|p array of 20 HPGe detectors with         
 62ZN5c  Compton-suppression and SCEPTAR array of plastic scintillators for |b  
 62ZN6c  particles. Deduced precise and accurate |b{++}+|e branch to            
 62ZN7c  g.s. of {+62}Zn and associated log {Ift} value relevant to             
 62ZN8c  superallowed |b decay from 0+ to 0+ state and breaking of isospin      
 62ZN9c  symmetry.                                                              
 62ZN c  2008Be21, 2005Ca06: {+62}Ga was produced in bombardment of {+64}Zn     
 62ZN2c  target by 48 MeV protons at IGISOL facility in Jyvaskyla. Fusion       
 62ZN3c  evaporation residues were thermalized in helium gas and singly-charged 
 62ZN4c  ions were mass analyzed. JYFLTRAP facility was used to separate {+62}Ga
 62ZN5c  from other isobaric activities. Penning-trap separated {+62}Ga was     
 62ZN6c  used for measurement of E|g and I|g. Different measurement cycles were 
 62ZN7c  used on the mass-separated source in another setup. Detection          
 62ZN8c  system consisted of three HPGe clover detectors (for |g rays), and 4|p 
 62ZN9c  cylindrical plastic scintillators for |b particles. Measured E|g, I|g, 
 62ZNAc  |g|g and |b|g coin. Half-life measurement in 2005Ca06                  
 62ZN c  2008Gr03: E=500 MeV protons produced at TRIUMF cyclotron. {+62}Ga beam 
 62ZN2c  produced using TRILIS. Measured |b particles using 4|p gas counter     
 62ZN3c  and 20 plastic scintillators. Detected |g rays with 8|p |g-ray         
 62ZN4c  spectrometer. Measured precise half-life of {+62}Ga decay              
 62ZN c  2006Hy02 (also 2005Hy04): {+62}Ga was produced in spallation reaction  
 62ZN2c  by 500 MeV protons on a ZrC target. Mass-separated 30-keV {+62}Ga beam 
 62ZN3c  was obtained using a laser ion source at TRIUMF-ISAC facility and      
 62ZN4c  implanted in a Mylar tape for |g and |b counting.                      
 62ZN5c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b, |b|g coin using 8|p array                 
 62ZN6c  of 20 Compton-suppressed HPGe detectors for |g rays and an array of 20 
 62ZN7c  plastic scintillators for |b rays. Half-life measurement is reported   
 62ZN8c  by 2005Hy04. Same group as 2008Fi07 and 2008Gr03                       
 62ZN c  2004Bl03: {+62}Ga from {+28}Si({+40}Ca,np|a) at GSI; measured          
 62ZN2c  half-life, |b|g coin                                                   
 62ZN c  2003Hy02: {+62}Ga from {+1}H({+64}Zn,3n) at 42 MeV/nucleon; measured   
 62ZN2c  E|g, I|g, half-life, branching ratios at the Texas A&M University K500 
 62ZN3c  Superconducting Cyclotron.                                             
 62ZN c  2002Lo13 (also 2002Bl17): {+62}Ga from fragmentation of {+78}Kr beam,  
 62ZN2c  GANIL facility, measured half-life                                     
 62ZN c  1993Wi18, 1993Wi03: {+58}Ni({+84}Kr,X) E=75 MeV/nucleon. Measured      
 62ZNxc  half-life using A1200 radioactive-beam facility at the NSCL-MSU.       
 62ZN c  1979Da04: from {+58}Ni({+6}Li,2n), E=25 MeV, |DE-E telescopes (plastic 
 62ZN2c  or semiconductors), T{-1/2}, Q(|e) at Argonne FN tandem accelerator.   
 62ZN c  1978Al23: from {+58}Ni({+6}Li,2n), E=25 MeV, plastic scintillator,     
 62ZNxc  half-life at Brookhaven National Laboratory.                           
 62ZN c  1978Ch11 (also 1973ChYF): from {+64}Zn(p,3n), E=44 MeV, plastic        
 62ZN2c  scintillator, Ge(Li), half-life, Q(|b{++}) at the synchrocyclotron of  
 62ZN3c  the Institute for Nuclear Study, University of Tokyo.                  
 62ZN c  1976BaXP: from Zn(p,3n), E=44 MeV, half-life at McGill University      
 62ZN2c  cyclotron facility                                                     
 62ZN c  1976JaZP: from {+46}Ti({+19}F,3n) and {+50}Cr({+16}O,p3n), plastic     
 62ZN2c  scintillator, half-life at Chalk-River tandem accelerator.             
 62ZN c  1973ChYF: from {+64}Zn(p,3n), E=32-52 MeV, plastic scintillator, Ge(Li)
 62ZN2c  at the synchrocyclotron of the Institute for Nuclear Study, University 
 62ZN3c  of Tokyo.                                                              
 62ZN c  2008Fi07, 2008Gr03, 2006Hy02 (also 2005Hy04) are from the same group   
 62ZN c  2008Be21, 2005Ca06, 2004Bl03, 2002Lo13 (also 2002Bl17) share some of   
 62ZN2c  the same authors, but some of the studies are at different facilities  
 62ZN c  Review of superallowed (0+ to 0+) |b decays: 2010To12, 2009Er02,       
 62ZN2c  2009Ha12, 2008To03, 2005Ha27, 2002Ha27; also 2006Ha12, 2005Ha15,       
 62ZN3c  2005Ha65 conference papers.                                            
 62ZN d  Theory: 2011Sa08 (log |{Ift} values)                                   
 62ZN d  2008FiZX superseded by 2008Fi07                                        
 62ZN d  2008GrZO superseded by 2008Gr03                                        
 62ZN d  2006HyZZ superseded by 2006Hy02                                        
 62ZN d  2000DoZX, 2000DoZZ, 2001DoZZ, 2003BlZZ, 2004CaZX superseded by         
 62ZN2d  2004Bl03 and 2005Ca06                                                  
 62ZN c  References and notes on half-life measurement of {+62}Ga decay:        
 62ZN c  2008Gr03: {+62}Ga beam from TRIUMF ISAC using resonant ionization      
 62ZN2c  laser ion source and mass separation, positron detection using 4|p     
 62ZN3c  continuous flow gas proportional counter. Yields and activities        
 62ZN4c  of {+62}Cu, {+62m}Co, {+62g}Co, {+62}Mn and {+62}Fe contaminants were  
 62ZN5c  estimated from |b|g coin. data. Systematic and statistical             
 62ZN6c  uncertainties described in detail.                                     
 62ZN c  2005Ca06: {+62}Ga beam from IGISOL at Jyvaskyla. Positron detection    
 62ZN2c  using 4|p cylindrical plastic scintillator. Presence of {+62}Cu        
 62ZN3c  activity was considered as a constant background. Systematic and       
 62ZN4c  statistical uncertainties described in detail.                         
 62ZN c  2004Bl03: {+62}Ga beam from {+28}Si({+40}Ca,|apn) at 4.84 MeV/nucleon  
 62ZN2c  at GSI facility. Mass-analyzed beam and positron detection using 4|p   
 62ZN3c  gas detector and |g by HPGe detector. {+62}Cu and {+62}Zn impurities   
 62ZN4c  were taken into account. Systematic and statistical uncertainties      
 62ZN5c  described in detail.                                                   
 62ZN c  2003Hy02: {+62}Ga beam from {+1}H({+64}Zn,3n) at 42 MeV/nucleon        
 62ZN2c  at Texas A&M facility. Mass-analyzed beam was 80-94% pure {+62}Ga.     
 62ZN3c  Positron detection using 4|p gas proportional chamber. {+58}Cu and     
 62ZN4c  {+54}Co impurities quantified. The |g spectrum was measured            
 62ZN5c  by HPGe detector. Maximum likelihood method. Uncertainty analysis not  
 62ZN6c  discussed fully.                                                       
 62ZN c  2002Lo13 (also 2002Bl17): {+62}Ga from fragmentation of {+78}Kr beam,  
 62ZN2c  GANIL facility, decay curve of |b{++} particles correlated with        
 62ZN3c  implants shown; no discussion of uncertainties                         
 62ZN c  Total decay energy of 9181.2 keV {I7} deduced (by RADLIST code) from   
 62ZN2c  proposed decay scheme is in agreement with the expected value of       
 62ZN3c  9181.1 keV {I4}, indicating that decay scheme is complete              
