 62ZN    28SI(36AR,2PG),40CA(28SI,A2PG)2012GE04,1998SV01         25NDS    202507
 62ZN  H TYP=FUL$AUT=Balraj Singh, Huang Xiaolong, and Wang Xianghan$           
 62ZN2 H CIT=NDS 204, 1 (2025)$CUT=30-Jun-2023$                                 
 62ZN c  2012Ge04 (also 2009Ge14 and thesis by J. Gellanki, Lund University     
 62ZN2c  (2011)): data given in these works are from four experiments           
 62ZN3c  mentioned below: Data set 1: {+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g): {+28}Si beam at  
 62ZN4c  E=122 MeV at the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. Target=0.5     
 62ZN5c  mg/cm{+2} {+40}Ca. Gamma rays were detected using the Gammasphere array
 62ZN6c  with 103 HPGe detectors, and particles were detected by the Microball  
 62ZN7c  4|p charged-particle detector array.                                   
 62ZN8c  Data set 2: {+28}Si({+36}Ar,2p|g): {+36}Ar beam at E|?140 MeV          
 62ZN9c  at Argonne National Laboratory. Three different experiments using the  
 62ZNAc  Gammasphere array were carried out. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,      
 62ZNBc  (particle)|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO). Deduced 262 levels from 460 |g rays, 
 62ZNCc  J|p, bands, multipolarities, mixing ratios of a few transitions, and   
 62ZNDc  configurations. Comparison with cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky             
 62ZNEc  calculations.                                                          
 62ZN c  1998Sv01, 1997Sv02, 1998SvZY: {+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g),E=115, 125 MeV.  
 62ZN2c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, (particle)|g|g-coin, level T{-1/2} by    
 62ZN3c  Doppler shift attenuation method. Two experiments were conducted, first
 62ZN4c  at Chalk River using the TASCC accelerator facility, and the second    
 62ZN4c  at LBNL, Berkeley cyclotron facility. First experiment used 8|p array  
 62ZN5c  of 20 Compton-suppressed Ge detectors and a 70-element BGO ball, with  
 62ZN6c  Miniball array of 44-element CsI(Tl) charged-particle detectors. The   
 62ZN7c  second experiment used Gammasphere array of 83 Compton-suppressed Ge   
 62ZN8c  detectors and Microball array of 95-element CsI(Tl) charged-particle   
 62ZN9c  detectors. Deduced extensive high-spin level scheme with six bands up  
 62ZNAc  to J|p=24, and one SD band. See also 1997Sv04 and 1998-Svensson, p407, 
 62ZNBc  ENAM98 conference proceedings (1998). These results are in general     
 62ZNCc  agreement with much more extensive band structures in 2012Ge04.        
 62ZN c  1997Fu08: {+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g),E=120 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g,        
 62ZN2c  |g|g-coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO) at the tandem accelerator of Japan Atomic     
 62ZN3c  Energy Agency using an array of ten Compton-suppressed Ge              
 62ZN4c  detectors and Si-ball for charged-particles. Only a level scheme is    
 62ZN5c  provided in the paper with |g-cascades:                                
 62ZN6c  2484-1585-1161-1791-1341-1177-1197-1521-1232-954; 1603-938-1804;       
 62ZN7c  1557-1073-913-2830, and some other levels, with a total of 38 |g rays  
 62ZN8c  and 26 excited levels of spins from 2 to 16 assigned for 12 levels.    
 62ZN9c  While the results are in general agreement with those from 1997Fu08    
 62ZNAc  and 2012Ge04, placements of six |g rays from six levels (3784 to 8331  
 62ZNBc  keV) in the level scheme were not confirmed in later studies.          
 62ZN d  1996FuZV superseded by 1997Fu08                                        
 62ZN c  1979Mu04 (also 1980MuZV thesis): {+40}Ca({+28}Si,|a2p|g),E=93.5, 102   
 62ZN2c  MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, |g(|q) and |g|g(|q)(DCO) using two  
 62ZN3c  Ge(Li) detectors at the University of Pennsylvania FN tandem Van de    
 62ZN4c  Graaff accelerator. (1161)-1341-1177-1197-1521-1232-954 and            
 62ZN5c  1177-557-1604-557-1232 |g-cascades proposed in this study, with        
 62ZN6c  nine excited states reported: 953.9, 2+; 2186.1, 4+; 2743.1, (3-,4+);  
 62ZN7c  3707.8, (6+); 4347.1; 4905.0, (7); 6081.9, (9); 7423.4, (11);          
 62ZN8c  (8594.2), (12). Except for the tentative placement of the 1161|g,      
 62ZN9c  ordering of the two cascades is in agreement with those in 1998Sv01    
 62ZNAc  2012Ge04                                                               
 62ZN c  All data here are from 2012Ge04 unless otherwise specified.            
 62ZN cG $The |g|g(|q)(DCO) data from 2012Ge04 are available for 30|'-83|',     
 62ZN2cG 30|'-53|', and 53|'-83|' geometries. Stated values in this dataset are 
 62ZN3cG mainly for 30|'-83|' geometry. For 30 |g rays, data are available for  
 62ZN4cG all the three geometries, where these are listed in the following      
 62ZN5cG order: the first DCO for 30|'-83|', second for 30|'-53|', and the      
 62ZN6cG third for 53|'-83|'. Expected DCO values are: 1.0, |?0.6, and 0.9      
 62ZN7cG corresponding to |DJ=2, quadrupole (likely E2); |DJ=1, dipole or       
 62ZN8cG dipole+quadrupole (likely M1+E2); and |DJ=0, dipole, respectively,     
 62ZN9cG when gated on known |DJ=2, quadrupole transitions                      
 62ZN cG E,RI$From 2012Ge04. Values available from other studies are listed     
 62ZN2cG under comments                                                         
 62ZN cG MR$From 2012Ge04. Authors use Rose-Brink convention. The sign here has 
 62ZN2cG been reversed to be consistent with Krane-Steffen convention used      
 62ZN3cG in ENSDF database                                                      
 62ZN cL $Levels at 7630 keV decaying by 1548|g, and 10317 keV, 13+ decaying by 
 62ZN2cL 851 and 1268 |g rays, and a |g ray of 3006 keV from 10636, 12(+) in    
 62ZN3cL 1998Sv01 were not confirmed by 2012Ge04, thus omitted here.            
 62ZN cL $Placements of six |g rays from six levels: 3784 (2830|g),             
 62ZN2cL 4697 (913|g), 5770 (1073|g), 7327 (1557|g), 7701 (279|g), and          
 62ZN3cL 8331 (909|g) were not confirmed in more detailed studies by 1998Sv01   
 62ZN4cL and 2012Ge04, thus omitted here.                                       
 62ZN cL $General specify configurations are listed in terms of valence holes   
 62ZN2cL or particles: [p{-1}(|+)p{-2},n{-1}(|+)n{-2}], where p{-1},            
 62ZN3cL n{-1}=number of proton or neutron holes in 1f{-7/2} orbital;           
 62ZN4cL p{-2}, n{-2}=number of neutron or proton particles in 1g{-9/2}         
 62ZN5cL orbital, relative to a closed {+56}Ni core.                            
 62ZN6cL The (|+) notation refers to |a=+1/2 and |a=-1/2 signature.             
 62ZN cL $Nothe that: configurations for bands are from Fig. 21 in 2012Ge04 in  
 62ZN2cL with the following nomenclature based on cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky    
 62ZN4cL formalism, and relative to {+56}Ni (N=Z=28) core:                      
 62ZN cL $|p[(1f{-7/2}){+-p1}(fp){+p3}(1g{-9/2}){+p2}] abbreviated as           
 62ZN2cL |p[p1,p2(|+)], where p3=2+p1-p2, + for |a=+1/2, - for |a=-1/2          
 62ZN3cL for odd number of {Ifp} protons p3.                                    
 62ZN cL $|n[(1f{-7/2}){+-n1}(fp){+n3}(1g{-9/2}){+n2}] abbreviated as           
 62ZN2cL |n[n1,n2(|+)], where n3=4+n1+n2, + for |a=+1/2, - for |a=-1/2          
 62ZN3cL for odd number of {Ifp} neutrons n3.                                   
 62ZN cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g data for 460 |g rays placed amongst    
 62ZN2cL 262 levels. Reduced |h{+2}=0.32, with only one |g ray poorly fitted.   
 62ZN cL E(Z)$No deexciting |g ray(s) from this level                           
 62ZN cL J$As given by 2012Ge04, based on multipolarity and |DJ assignments     
 62ZN2cL from |g|g(|q)(DCO) data, and band assignments.                         
