 62GA c  Study of the Triplet Energy Differences (TED) of A=62 triplet via two  
 62GA2c  neutron knockout from {+64}Ga, and also one-proton and two-neutron     
 62GA3c  removal from {+65}Ge                                                   
 62GA c  2015He22: A cocktail of secondary beams including {+64}Ga and {+65}Ge  
 62GA2c  were produced by fragmentation of E=150 MeV/nucleon primary beam of    
 62GA3c  {+78}Kr from the Coupled Cyclotron Facility at NSCL on a 650 mg/cm{+2} 
 62GA4c  beryllium target. Fragments were identified and selected by the A1900  
 62GA5c  fragment separator and incident on a secondary target of 96 mg/cm{+2}  
 62GA6c  Be foil. Reaction products were identified in the S800 spectrometer;   
 62GA7c  The |g rays were detected using the GRETINA array with 28 coaxial HPGe 
 62GA8c  crystals. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, ({+62}Ga recoils)|g-coin.      
 62GA9c  Deduced levels, J|p, isospin. Comparison with shell-model              
 62GAAc  calculations.                                                          
