 62GA c  Dataset adapted from a dataset in the XUNDL database from 2020Ru03     
 62GA2c  compiled by E.A. McCutchan (NNDC,BNL), March 1, 2021.                  
 62GA c  2020Ru03: E({+28}Si)=122 MeV. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin,            
 62GA2c  |g|g(|q)(DCO), (particle)|g-coin using the Gammasphere array consisting
 62GA3c  of 101 HPGe detectors and the Microball 4|p array of 95 element CsI(Tl)
 62GA4c  detectors at the ATLAS-ANL facility. Target was 99.975% enriched       
 62GA5c  {+40}Ca with a thickness of 0.5 mg/cm{+2}. Deduced high-spin rotational
 62GA6c  states, and interpreted in terms of cranked Nilsson-Strutinsky         
 62GA7c  calculations, with proposed configurations.                            
 62GA cG $DCO ratios are for 30|' and 83|' geometry. With gates on |DJ=2,       
 62GA2cG quadrupole transitions (946.2, 1107.4, 1240.9, 1387.4, 1745.8, 2354.8),
 62GA3cG expected ratios are: |?0.6 for |DJ=1, dipole, and 1.0 for |DJ=2,       
 62GA4cG quadrupole transitions. Lower or higher DCO values as compared to |?0.6
 62GA5cG for |DJ=1, dipole suggest mixed |DJ=1, D+Q (generally M1+E2)           
 62GA6cG transitions. Less frequent |DJ=0, dipole transitions are expected to   
 62GA7cG have DCO|?0.9.                                                         
