 62GE c  2002Lo13 (Also 2002Bl17): {+62}Ge observed in fragmentation of {+78}Kr 
 62GE2c  beam at 73 MeV/nucleon using LISE3 spectrometer at GANIL facility.     
 62GE3c  Isotopic identification by time-of-flight and energy loss methods.     
 62GE4c  Measured isotopic half-life by decay timing of correlated |b{++}       
 62GE5c  (ion implant) events and energy loss vs time-of-flight                 
 62GE c  2005St29 (also 2005St34): {+62}Ge observed in fragmentation of {+78}Kr 
 62GE2c  beam at 140 MeV/nucleon with a {+9}Be target using A1900 spectrometer  
 62GE3c  at NSCL, MSU. Measured cross section=4.8 nb {I20}                      
 62GE c  2007Bl09: {+62}Ge observed in fragmentation of {+70}Ge beam            
 62GE2c  at 71.6 MeV/nucleon with a Ni target using LISE3 spectrometer          
 62GE3c  at GANIL facility                                                      
 62GE c  2014Gr10: study of Gamow-Teller decay of T=1, J|p=0+ {+62}Ge g.s. to   
 62GE2c  N=Z {+62}Ga nucleus. The {+62}Ge source was formed in fragmentation of 
 62GE3c  750 MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr beam impinging a {+9}Be target, followed by    
 62GE4c  B|r-|DE-B|r and time-of-flight analysis by using FRS fragment separator
 62GE5c  and various scintillation and ionization detectors. The ions of {+62}Ga
 62GE6c  were implanted into a pack of six 1 mm thick double-sided silicon strip
 62GE7c  detectors (DSSSDs). Measured E|g, I|g, (particle)|g-coin, (fragment)|b-
 62GE8c  and |b|g-coin, half-life of {+62}Ge ground state.                      
 62GE c  2014Ro14: {+62}Ge isotope produced in the fragmentation of             
 62GE2c  70 MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr beam with Ni target. Fragments selected using   
 62GE3c  the LISE3 separator at GANIL and identified by time-of-flight and      
 62GE4c  energy loss. Measured half-life of {+62}Ge ground-state decay by       
 62GE5c  (fragment)|b, (fragment)|g correlations using four Si detectors        
 62GE6c  (an energy loss |DE detector, a degrade, DSSD and Si(Li)) for particles
 62GE7c  surrounded by four HPGe Clover detectors, three EXOGAM and one         
 62GE8c  mini-clover Ge detector for |g rays.                                   
 62GE c  2017Ku12: {+62}Ge isotope produced in the fragmentation of             
 62GE2c  79 MeV/nucleon {+64}Zn{+29+} beam with Ni target of 236 mg/cm{+2}      
 62GE3c  thickness. Fragments were selected with the LISE3 separator at         
 62GE4c  GANIL and identified by time-of-flight and energy loss using silicon   
 62GE5c  |DE detector and implanted into a double-sided silicon strip           
 62GE6c  detector (DSSSD). The implanted ions and charged-particle decays       
 62GE7c  were detected by the DSSSD, which was surrounded by four HPGe Clover   
 62GE8c  detectors (three EXOGAM clovers and a smaller Euroball clover)         
 62GE9c  for |g-ray detection. Half-life of {+62}Ge decay was measured by       
 62GEAc  ({+62}Ge implants)|b time-correlated decay events.                     
 62GEBc  Total number of {+62}Ge implanted ions=6080                            
 62GE c  2021Or01: E=345 MeV/nucleon {+78}Kr was produced at RIBF-RIKEN facility
 62GE2c  Fragments were separated, selected and identified by the BigRIPS       
