 62SE c  2016Bl05: {+62}Se nuclide was searched for at the RIBF-RIKEN facility  
 62SE2c  in {+9}Be({+78}Kr,X) fragmentation reaction at E=345 MeV/nucleon with  
 62SE3c  an intensity of up to 250 pnA. The target thickness was 5 and 7 mm     
 62SE4c  for settings on different nuclei. Fragments were separated on the      
 62SE5c  basis of |DE-tof-B|r method using BigRIPS separator. The separated     
 62SE6c  nuclei were transmitted to the Zero-Degree spectrometer (ZDS) and      
 62SE7c  implanted in a stack of double-sided silicon-strip detectors (WAS3ABi  
 62SE8c  setup), surrounded by EURICA array of HPGe detectors. 2016Bl05 state   
 62SE9c  that detailed spectroscopic investigations will be reported            
 62SEac  elsewhere. In the current paper, main emphasis is on determination of  
 62SEbc  production cross sections for several new isotopes with settings       
 62SEcc  optimized for {+51}Ni, {+62}Se, {+64}Se and {+65}Br. Comparison of     
 62SEdc  measured cross sections with theoretical calculations using LISE++     
 62SEec  and LIESCHEN computer codes, and compared with EPAX3 predictions       
 62SE c  Theoretical calculations: consult the NSR database at                  
 62SE2c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/ for four primary references for nuclear          
 62SE3c  structure and six for 2p decay mode and half-life calculations         
